              "alt": "What makes the Sense Maker Data Collector different?\n#context #nonlinear"
            },
            {
              "href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DBroB3KslXX/",
              "image": "/media/image-asset-7aee9cbc.jpg",
              "alt": "Marginalised people are treated unfairly because of prejudices. Their voices are often not heard in policy-making. This so called epistemic injustice leads to dismissed knowledge and lack of understanding in case of missing language and frameworks. E"
            },
            {
              "href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DBmZl4aMhlU/",
              "image": "/media/image-asset-c32d0c19.jpg",
              "alt": "We use abduction as reasoning method to perform sense making. It helps us dealing with ambiguity about human behaviour. By questioning the assumptions and seeking more contextual information such as personal stories, we are able to see and understand"
